  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want blacklisted members' posts hidden or collapsed and whitelisted ones highlighted, so that I read what I care about.\n\n### Scope\n\nPure visibility policy (BL/WL, hide pseudo setting, posts quoting me highlighted via LOT-032) applied by the HTML builder; a hidden post can still be revealed and reported (p. 458).\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: Phase 4 backlog 'visibility policy (BL/WL/filters, C10)'; user feedback 'highlight posts that quote me'\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `Classes/BlackList.m`, `Classes/ObjCTopicHTMLRenderer.m`, `Common.swift` (love/action colours), `AppSettingsView.swift:477` (`hideBlacklistedPseudo`)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-117-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-061 (#86, done)\n- LOT-083 (#101, done)\n- LOT-032 (#59, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged (unblocked 2026-10-29, steward ext/opus-helper1)\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Policy is a pure function with tests per case; a blacklisted post can still be alerted.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
